,title,link,text,language,family
0,Contact (2009 film) - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contact_(2009_film),Contact is a 2009 Australian documentary film that tells the story of 20 Martu people who in 1964 became the last people in the Great Sandy Desert to have come into contact with Europeans.,Martu Wangka,Australian
1,Martu Wangka dialect - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martu_Wangka_dialect,Martu Wangka is a variety of the Western Desert language that emerged during the 20th century in Western Australia as several Indigenous communities shifted from their respective territories to form a single community.,Martu Wangka,Australian
2,Martu Wangka - Mamala Wanalku Kuju Wankalpayi - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=grLqp5R_uHk,"Dec 18, 2024 · Martu Wangka - Mamala Wanalku Kuju Wankalpayi Languages in Australia 45 subscribers Subscribe",Martu Wangka,Australian
3,GRN Martu Wangka - Martu Wangka - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLURSoBcThm8xuvUVgn-XTkDMblSBY5Ed8,GRN recordings in Martu Wangka - Martu Wangka These recordings are designed for evangelism and basic Bible teaching to bring the gospel message to people who...,Martu Wangka,Australian
4,Martu Wangka language - Global Recordings Network,https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/mpj,"Audio recordings available in Martu Wangka These recordings are designed for evangelism and basic Bible teaching to bring the gospel message to people who are not literate or are from oral cultures, particularly unreached people groups.",Martu Wangka,Australian
5,Martu Wangka | Wangka Maya Pilbara Aboriginal Language Centre,https://www.wangkamaya.org.au/pilbara-languages/martu-wangka,Martu Wangka is a relatively strong language and is in widespread use on the Martu lands in the Western Desert region of the Pilbara. It is often the first language of Aboriginal children in their communities.,Martu Wangka,Australian
6,26-531 – Zekkiah Anderson - Martumili Artists Online Store,https://gallery.martumili.com.au/product/26-531-zekkiah-anderson/,"The traditional lands of the Martu people encompass the Great Sandy Desert and Rudall River regions of Western Australia, and include speakers of Manyjilyjarra, Warnman, Kartujarra, Putijarra and Martu Wangka languages. Since the 1980’s Return to Country movement, many Martu have chosen to live in remote Aboriginal Communities, including Punmu, Parnngurr, Kunawarritji, Jigalong, Irrungadji ...",Martu Wangka,Australian
7,Martu Wangka | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/mpj/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..ta9AGZT8IxCyDKvhM_L11hhPjnDneA3vwBX66TolL54,Martu Wangka is a stable indigenous language of Australia. It belongs to the Australian language family.,Martu Wangka,Australian
8,Pilbara Languages | Wangka Maya Pilbara Aboriginal Language Centre,https://www.wangkamaya.org.au/pilbara-languages/01-martu-wangka,"In 2005, Wangka Maya published the Martu Wangka Dictionary, which can also be seen in an on-line version. The dictionary was based on work done by Martu speaker Joshua Booth with linguist James Marsh and also includes material compiled by Ken Hansen.",Martu Wangka,Australian
9,"Full text of ""Martu Wangka Description""",https://archive.org/stream/rosettaproject_mpj_desc-1/rosettaproject_mpj_desc-1_djvu.txt,"Martu Wangka or a closely related dialect is spoken by some 800-1,000 people in and around the Gibson and Great Sandy Desert area of Western Australia. The communities where a significant number of Martu Wangka speakers live are Jigalong, Parnngurr, Punmu, Purntawari...",Martu Wangka,Australian
